unipicker searches Unicode characters by description using a
configurable selector and optionally copies the selected character
to the clipboard.
Interactive selection needs a selector command. The default is fzf,
but rofi or another command can be used instead. The --list option
does not need a selector.

Optional dependencies:
  fzf (https://slackbuilds.org/apps/fzf/) for the default selector.
  xclip (https://slackbuilds.org/apps/xclip/) for X11 clipboard support.
  rofi (https://slackbuilds.org/apps/rofi/) as an alternative selector.

Configure system defaults in /etc/unipickerrc or personal overrides in
~/.unipickerrc. For example, use rofi with:

  unipicker --command "rofi -dmenu"

Use --copy to copy the selection with xclip, or --copy-command to select
another clipboard command. Without these options, the character is only
printed to standard output. A UTF-8 locale and a font containing the
desired characters are recommended.

This package uses the symbol data bundled with the upstream release.
See /usr/doc/unipicker-<version>/README.md for usage and configuration.
